family objects and front-door consolidation (decided, VD 2026-09-08;
  docs/decisions.md dec-B98)
  pre-release: family accepts a token or a family object carrying its
  settings (hazard(breaks, max.rows), nbinom(dispersion), later aft and
  others); the three family-only formals leave bart with tombstones;
  audit every remaining front-door formal and move family-only or
  feature-only ones onto their objects (the August consolidation left
  these); fold resid.dist into the family objects (Student-t errors as
  a variant or setting), retiring dbartsResidDists, else export it to
  match dbartsPriors (dec-B101). Plan doc to write; lands with the
  front-door rename.

remove the posterior dependency (decided, VD 2026-09-08;
  docs/decisions.md dec-B99)
  pre-release: drop posterior from DESCRIPTION; summary computes split
  R-hat and effective sample size in R/diagnostics.R itself; replace
  the as_draws methods with a base-R draws extractor (iterations x
  chains x variables array with dimnames, the layout posterior's
  as_draws_array accepts); rewrite the five tinytest files and the
  summary man page that call posterior. Matrix and survival stay
  Suggests (recommended packages). Principle (VD): no bad
  dependencies - recommended packages, or ones that understand less is
  more.

sparse factors on the formula interface (decided, VD 2026-09-08;
  docs/decisions.md dec-B100)
  pre-release, R layer: a sparse() formula term (y ~ a + sparse(g)),
  stripped before the model frame like forest() terms; the argument is
  a factor column dbarts converts or an existing sparse object. Chosen
  from docs/plans/sparse-formula-audit.md (no surveyed package carries
  a sparse block through a formula; model.frame refuses S4 columns).
  Plan doc to write.

