    branch; revisit these checks then.
  re-verify all four sister packages (stan4bart, treatSens, bartCause,
    bairrtt) against the final re-baked dbarts.h once, at the freeze.
    The reshape is the last planned pre-release breaking change, and
    the C ABI constants (DBARTS_C_API_MAJOR/MINOR) read 1.0 through the
    window and become the initial contract at this release.
  push dbarts 1.0-0 (branch bartcore) and stan4bart 0.0-14; submit both
    to CRAN together. bartCause releases from its dbarts-1.0 branch,
    re-verified against the final header at the freeze.
  drop DBARTS_REQUIRE_EXACT_ABI from stan4bart (src/Makevars.in,
    src/Makevars.win) and treatSens (src/R_interface.cpp,
    src/bartTreatmentModel.cpp, src/sensitivityAnalysis.cpp) at the
    coordinated 1.0 merge.
  close GitHub issue #80 at release: the setResponse updateScale switch
    resolves it - default FALSE locks the creation-time prior scale,
    the safe embedded-Gibbs behavior the issue asks for, and latent
    families never rescale by construction. Point the reporter at the
    dbartsSampler-class.Rd and NEWS entries.
  on any post-release dbarts.h change: bump DBARTS_C_API_MINOR (or MAJOR
    if incompatible) alongside the hash re-bake, and bump stan4bart's
    Depends/LinkingTo dbarts floor in the same lockstep release - the
    load handshake covers the library-ahead direction, the floor covers
    consumer-ahead; both must move together.
  optional courtesy: notify the tmle maintainers. Their default
    SuperLearner dbarts wrappers pass obsWeights unconditionally and
    pnorm() the latents; unit weights are handled dbarts-side now, but
    genuinely weighted binomial analyses lose the dbarts learners by
    design, and family routing on their side would need the matching
    inverse link.
